9 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined-3small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined-3small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5318014032">February 25, 2023</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">I really wanted to love this one. The synopsis made the story seem cute and all the positive reviews made me excited to pick this book up, but unforunately The Lady and the Rabbit fell flat for me.<br /><br />Laura Greenwood’s writing style felt very formal and dull. It was like I was reading an essay written for a college class instead of reading a nicely flowing book. I understand that some of this book needed to be formal because of the dynamics between the characters, but it felt a bit overdone.<br /><br />I also didn’t feel like there was much chemistry between George and Denise. Their interests made it seem like they would be a good fit for each other, but they had no connection and chemistry. It made me feel like their relationship wouldn’t be fulfilling for either of them in the long run.<br /><br />There was no major conflict in this story, which made this story slightly boring. The characters tried to act like there was something getting in the way of their marriage, but there really wasn’t. Everyone was on board with them marrying right away.<br /><br />I think Laura Greenwood’s books will work for some people, but this one u