stid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">I really really love this series! I quite enjoy reading about dating in the victorian era, with all the written and unwritten rules and all the gossip and talk about status. However, a lot of novels that are actually written at the time are a little too slow and too boring for me. I'm glad Greenwood gives me stories fitting me better and I was happy when BookSprout notified me that this book was available.<br /><br />What I loved most about this book is the playfulness of the characters and the creative ways they find to break the rules. Love was not the standard at the time and I'm glad that in these novels people are actually marrying the person they want to marry most. Even if they have to sneak to balconies to talk or have to smuggle a rabbit into the library for some privacy.<br /><br />I also really enjoy how beautifully the stories of the two sisters intertwine. Even though we see glimpses of this story in the story of the sister and the other way round, they don't give the complete picture of each other's story. I therefore really enjoyed seeing some bits and pieces of story I already loved, but I enjoyed it even more to finally get the full story of these two characters!<br /><br />While reading this book it also felt like I was reading about a version of myself. Who I would have been if I had been stuck in this era and was forced to find a suitable partner. Although I love company and dancing a little more than our heroine, I do agree it's a horrible way to get to know a romantic partner. And I do also prefer the company of some good books!</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/11358898?shelf=review-copies" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">review-copies</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer cla