6C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined0small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined0small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5111629187">November 18, 2022</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Denise and George were getting to know one another in the background of Victoria's story, but here they come front and center, allowing us to not only truly enjoy their relationship, but to see several scenes from another perspective than we did before.<br /><br />George is a good, honest shifter... and he's about to learn not to sell himself short.<br /><br />This done in one quick read is a nice story about how we get to know people, the things that guide our thinking and assumptions, and the wonderful things that can come from communication.<br /><br />"I do not see how it is possible to find a husband by dancing.".<br /><br />I was gifted with a copy of the Lady and the Rabbit and chose to share my thoughts.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">1 like</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review un